- Story & Context: Legend says that if you turn the gain on the main pipe-valve to the exact point of structural failure, the ghosts of the old city will speak through the feedback of the radiator. Mura stood by the valve as the entire floor shook, watching the steam turn into a blinding, golden fog that seemed to swallow the encroaching tide whole. "Listen close, the metal remembers the heat of the hearth," she shouted over the roar of the machine, a myth born in the moment the roof began to collapse under the weight of the rain.
